 ## Background
-Originating from the need to accelerate Feldkamp-Davis-Kress (FDK) and parallel-beam reconstruction algorithms, GPU-based back-projection became standard with the advent of OpenCL and CUDA. The specific implementations cited rely on OpenCL for cross-vendor compatibility. The use of image textures for interpolation exploits dedicated GPU hardware units, reducing arithmetic intensity [5111-gpu-backprojection-using-opencl-image-textures.md](5111-gpu-backprojection-using-opencl-image-textures.md).
